{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\mathcal{F} : & (\\Sch/S)^{opp} & \\longrightarrow & \\textit{Ab} \\\\\n& T/S & \\longmapsto & \\Gamma(T, \\Omega_{T/S}).\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\Spec(\\mathbf{F}_p)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\varphi :\nV = \\Spec(\\mathbf{F}_p[v])\n\\to\nU = \\Spec(\\mathbf{F}_p[u])\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$v^p$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{\\varphi\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(V)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\text{d}u$", "MATH_0010": "$\\text{d}(v^p) = 0$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}(U) \\ar[r]^{0} &\n\\mathcal{F}(V) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}(V \\times_U V)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:90f89032396a06bb064d133196691655e8aa8b85ecf8e54f55a21110f16beb27", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:977736ad21ee229a32803188c905973ea43d10911978bd692a9c2712d656c208", "source_text": "Consider the presheaf\n<MATH_0001>\nThe compatibility of differentials with localization implies that\n<MATH_0002> is a sheaf on the Zariski site.\nHowever, it does not satisfy the sheaf condition for the fpqc topology.\nNamely, consider the case\n<MATH_0003> and the morphism\n<MATH_0004>\ngiven by mapping <MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>. The family <MATH_0007> is an fpqc covering,\nyet the restriction mapping\n<MATH_0008>\nsends the generator <MATH_0009> to <MATH_0010>, so\nit is the zero map, and the diagram\n<MATH_0011>\nis not an equalizer. We will see later that <MATH_0012> does in fact\ngive rise to a sheaf on the <ACCENT_0001>tale and smooth sites.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7541c2bd6cbab03ef4713d455a2622ec604283884b89554251a2831d63e7c1d7", "unit_id": "tag:03O2:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch/S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-sheaf-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0d67f5e5978135c97ead8ea4db423eee7e2adf9638db7bda7d83fb411b27c72b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7631c882bd5d5f35b61406f36180573a84604d99cf8525b7d2de8932caa6409b", "source_text": "Any representable presheaf on <MATH_0001> satisfies the\nsheaf condition for the fpqc topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4ebc5a39efd120ee53b03b6d71634ec6b311e13ac183388adce5c50d44caabe2", "unit_id": "tag:03O3:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-lemma-fpqc-universal-effective-epimorphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5cbcb212cfe7f2323826d12b869ad3f81c2a3e5fa456ae78d89fcca78fdba5b", "source_text": "See\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:41c41663e9db65846d2a545e30e3014807c6548419067fbd069906c32dfd196f", "unit_id": "tag:03O3:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-section-representable-sheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:77941c0618cb62a2bc7773832ed9469cd03737470e18af0b6cede59dfdca6e54", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will return to this later, since the proof of this fact uses\ndescent for quasi-coherent sheaves, which we will discuss in the next\nsection. A fancy way of expressing the lemma is to say that\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>the fpqc topology is weaker than the canonical topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or\nthat the fpqc topology is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>subcanonical<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>. In the setting of sites\nthis is discussed in\nSites, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e669b6bd88b57f8e0eb3e81d36fb050a98536247dbe64618121298191930d44e", "unit_id": "tag:03NV:prose-0005"}
